    controlFlow:
      "Control flow refers to the order in which individual statements are executed. In nested if statements, control flow follows a depth-first pattern: the outer condition is checked first, and if true, control enters the outer block where the next condition is checked. This creates a sequential filtering effect — each level acts as a filter that only passes control deeper if its condition is satisfied.",
